If I may be permitted to add my 2 sous here, I would like to say
that although I agree with RS's answer, I do regard it as a definite
defect in tex (not plain, not latex, but tex) that a tex primitive
depend on another tex primitive when the latter can be redefined.
If \vfill were a \def'ined term, then you could \let\Par\par and
then redefine \vfill using \Par.  But the dependency is built in and
cannot be overcome so easily.

Michael Barr

